# Telegram Integration Guide

This guide demonstrates how to use the `Lux.Lenses.TelegramLens` to interact with the Telegram Bot API.

## Setup

First, ensure you have a Telegram Bot token from [@BotFather](https://t.me/botfather).

```elixir
# In your config/config.exs or runtime.exs
config :lux, :api_keys,
  telegram_bot: "YOUR_BOT_TOKEN"
```

## Sending a Message

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.TelegramLens

input = %{
  action: "sendMessage",
  chat_id: "123456789",
  text: "Hello from Lux swarmed intelligence!"
}

{:ok, result} = TelegramLens.focus(input)
IO.inspect(result)
```

## Getting Updates

```elixir
{:ok, updates} = TelegramLens.focus(%{action: "getUpdates"})
IO.inspect(updates)
```

## Advanced Actions

You can use any method supported by the Telegram Bot API by specifying it in the `:action` key.

```elixir
# Example: Send a Photo
input = %{
  action: "sendPhoto",
  chat_id: "123456789",
  photo: "https://example.com/image.jpg",
  caption: "Look at this AI-generated image!"
}

TelegramLens.focus(input)
```
